# vram-fit — rules for AI coding agents (Cursor, Windsurf, Claude Code, Copilot, OpenHands)

## If the user has a GPU-memory problem, use the tool — don't guess
- Symptoms: "CUDA out of memory", "torch.OutOfMemoryError", "ggml_cuda ... out of memory", "failed to allocate buffer",
  Ollama "requires more system memory", vLLM "No available memory for the cache blocks", "will this model fit",
  "how much VRAM", "which quant", "what -ngl", "max context", "LoRA/QLoRA batch size".
- Run (always with --json, always with --gpu):
    vram-fit fit <hf-repo-or-gguf> --gpu auto -c <context> --json            # best config + launch command
    vram-fit estimate <model> --gpu <preset> -q <quant> -c <ctx> --kv 8 --json
    vram-fit fit <repo> --mode qlora --engine unsloth -c <seq> --gpu auto --json
- Parse result.status (fits|tight|offload|spill|oom), result.gpu_total_mib, result.segments[], result.performance,
  and for `fit`: result.command.shell / result.command.files. Schema: schema.json. Full guide: AGENT_GUIDE.md.
- Never download model weights just to test whether they fit.

## Working on this codebase
- Layout: src/vram_fit/{hub,gguf,ggml,model,quant,estimator,optimizer,commands,hardware,presets,catalog,render,cli,server}.py
- The core package is dependency-free (stdlib only). Only server.py may import fastapi/uvicorn. psutil is optional.
- Python >= 3.9: no `match`, no `X | Y` type unions at runtime, no nested same-quote f-strings.
- Units: bytes internally, MiB (2**20) in outputs; keys end in _mib / _gbs / _tok_s.
- estimate() must stay < 1 ms without `limits` (the dashboard calls it on every slider frame); cache per-model work in
  weights_profile(), keep everything else O(layers).
- Every CLI subcommand must support --json and print exactly one JSON document to stdout (errors included, exit 2).
  If you add or change output fields, update schema.json and the JSON tests in tests/test_cli_server.py.
- New quantization: add a QuantScheme in quant.py (+ tensor_bytes rule), aliases, tests against a real file size.
- New GPU: add to PRESETS in presets.py with vendor-rated bandwidth and dense FP16 tensor TFLOPS (fp32 accumulate).
- New architecture quirk: handle it in spec_from_hf_config / model_from_gguf and synthesize_inventory; add a param-count
  test against the model card.
- Generated commands (commands.py) must be real, runnable flags for current llama.cpp / Ollama / vLLM / TabbyAPI /
  Unsloth / TRL; every flag gets a {"flag", "why"} explanation.
- No TODOs, mocks or placeholder functions in src/. Tests use real code paths (a local HTTP Range server for the Hub).
- Run `pytest -q` and `python -m pyflakes src tests` before committing.
- After changing docs or CLI flags, run `python scripts/build_llms_full.py` to refresh llms-full.txt.
